  35: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  36:     """
  37:     Complete a sparse grid by casting occluding diagonal rays from the longest run and filling the remaining diagonal-connected regions from the short bars.
  38: 
  39:     Input structure
  40:     - Black-background grid with one unique longest 4-connected foreground object.
  41:     - The longest object is a horizontal or vertical multicolor run; all other foreground objects are shorter monochrome bars.
  42: 
  43:     Rule
  44:     - On a blank canvas, process the longest run from left to right or top to bottom; each pixel emits four 45-degree rays that stop at the first already-painted pixel.
  45:     - Each remaining monochrome bar fills every still-blank pixel reachable from it by diagonal steps.
  46: 
  47:     Key insight
  48:     - Earlier pixels in the long run occlude later diagonal rays, and those ray barriers partition the background into diagonal-connected regions for the short bars.
  49:     """
